{
  "title": "Piano Practice",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Read",
      "lines": [
        "Notes scroll right to",
        "left on a treble staff.",
        "Play the pad as the note",
        "crosses the line.",
        "",
        "On time: the notehead",
        "turns into a circle.",
        "Missed: it turns into",
        "an X.",
        "",
        "A circle also marks where",
        "you actually played. In",
        "time, it lands on the",
        "note as one mark. Late,",
        "you see two and the gap",
        "is your error.",
        "",
        "Miss a note and the",
        "scroll stops and names",
        "it on screen. With Guide",
        "pads on, the pad you",
        "need pulses white.",
        "",
        "Miss a note and the",
        "scroll stops on it. The X",
        "stays by the line however",
        "far ahead you are reading."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Levels",
      "lines": [
        "A song has up to four",
        "levels. Pick the song,",
        "then pick the level.",
        "",
        "L1 RH melody",
        "  the right hand alone,",
        "  one note at a time.",
        "L1 LH bass",
        "  the left hand alone,",
        "  the bass line.",
        "L2 RH chords",
        "  the melody with its",
        "  chords under it.",
        "L3 Both hands",
        "  the two together.",
        "",
        "All four sit in the same",
        "register. The pads you",
        "learn at L1 are the pads",
        "you play at L3.",
        "",
        "Back from a song goes to",
        "its levels, not all the",
        "way out to the songs.",
        "",
        "A drill with nothing to",
        "split shows one level,",
        "or arms straight away."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Guess",
      "lines": [
        "Three extra modes, from",
        "the top of the exercise",
        "list.",
        "Guess: notes / chords",
        "One note or chord sits",
        "still on the staff, named",
        "below it, until you play",
        "it. No clock, no timing.",
        "",
        "Hear: notes / chords",
        "The same, but you hear it",
        "instead of seeing it. The",
        "staff shows a ? until you",
        "play it right, then it",
        "reveals what it was.",
        "",
        "Both drill finding a",
        "pitch on the grid, which",
        "is its own skill: the",
        "pads go up in fifths, so",
        "the same note sits in",
        "several places.",
        "",
        "A chord must be held all",
        "at once. Part of it down",
        "is not yet a mistake.",
        "",
        "Pick: notes / chords",
        "A pad lights and you name",
        "it, choosing one of three",
        "with the jog. Click to",
        "answer. The other two are",
        "near misses - a semitone",
        "away, or the same chord",
        "root with another quality",
        "- so a rough sense of",
        "high or low will not do.",
        "",
        "This is the only mode",
        "that goes pad to name,",
        "and the only one you can",
        "do without playing.",
        "",
        "PLAY   hear it",
        "REC    help, twice",
        "BACK   back to the list",
        "",
        "Half tones adds the black",
        "notes to the note pools.",
        "On by default: they are",
        "the hard ones to find.",
        "",
        "Chords: triads asks the",
        "diatonic triads of the",
        "key. types asks a chosen",
        "quality - dim, aug, sus,",
        "6, 7, maj7, m7, m7b5,",
        "dim7, add9. advanced adds",
        "ninths and altered",
        "dominants: 9, maj9, m9,",
        "6/9, 7b5, 7#5, 7b9, 7#9,",
        "7sus4, 9sus4, mMaj7.",
        "",
        "Both the chord symbol and",
        "its notes are shown, so",
        "you learn what the shape",
        "under your hands is",
        "called. A scale that",
        "stacks something that is",
        "not a chord shows the",
        "notes with no symbol.",
        "",
        "The answer is never lit",
        "on the pads. Guide pads is",
        "a playing aid, not a",
        "hint for a quiz.",
        "",
        "REC gives help, two",
        "presses deep. Hearing:",
        "names it, then lights the",
        "pads. Reading: sounds it,",
        "then lights the pads.",
        "Picking: strikes out one",
        "wrong option, then the",
        "other.",
        "",
        "Hinted answers still count",
        "and keep the streak, but",
        "the round records how many",
        "you took."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rounds",
      "lines": [
        "A quiz is a round of 20",
        "prompts (10/20/30 in",
        "settings, or endless).",
        "",
        "The clock starts on your",
        "first press, not when the",
        "screen appears. A prompt",
        "waits until you get it",
        "right, so a wrong answer",
        "costs you time rather",
        "than a penalty - the same",
        "way a typing test treats",
        "a typo.",
        "",
        "The result is correct",
        "answers per minute, your",
        "error rate, and a chart",
        "of recent rounds.",
        "",
        "Progress, at the top of",
        "the list, plots one drill:",
        "the rate as a line, errors",
        "as bars under it. A full",
        "bar is 50% wrong.",
        "",
        "Jog changes drill. Rates",
        "only compare within a",
        "drill - hearing 7th chords",
        "is not naming a white note",
        "",
        "endless records nothing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Play",
      "lines": [
        "PLAY   listen. The",
        "  exercise plays itself",
        "  and the pads light up",
        "  as it goes, so you can",
        "  watch it before you",
        "  try it. Nothing scored.",
        "REC    practice. You",
        "  play it, it scores you.",
        "",
        "Both pulse when ready.",
        "The one that is running",
        "goes solid.",
        "",
        "JOG    pick, in the list",
        "CLICK  open the list",
        "MENU   open the list",
        "BACK   up one level",
        "SHIFT + BACK   close",
        "",
        "shift + jog: settings",
        "",
        "Four beats count you in,",
        "counted on screen."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sound",
      "lines": [
        "The module has its own",
        "piano. It is the default",
        "and needs no setup: no",
        "track, no instrument, no",
        "MIDI channel to match.",
        "It mixes in alongside",
        "whatever else Move is",
        "playing.",
        "",
        "MIDI out can send",
        "elsewhere instead:",
        "track  a Move track,",
        "  on the MIDI ch below",
        "  (all = every channel)",
        "USB    the USB-A port",
        "trk+USB  both of those",
        "",
        "Closing silences the",
        "piano and every channel",
        "on both MIDI routes,",
        "then waits for it to",
        "drain before letting go.",
        "SHIFT + BACK closes",
        "from anywhere."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Settings",
      "lines": [
        "SHIFT + CLICK opens",
        "settings. CLICK a row to",
        "edit it, turn to change,",
        "CLICK again when done.",
        "",
        "Wait stops the scroll at",
        "a note until you play it.",
        "On by default.",
        "",
        "The scroll always halts",
        "ON the note it wants,",
        "so you can see what it",
        "is asking for. A missed",
        "chord is named under",
        "the staff, not over it.",
        "",
        "PLAY again pauses where",
        "you are. Paused, knob 1",
        "scrubs - smoothly, about",
        "half a turn per bar.",
        "PLAY again carries",
        "on from there, so you",
        "can take a bar twice.",
        "BACK restarts; twice",
        "leaves. Knob 8 is tempo.",
        "",
        "Grace is how late you",
        "may play it and still",
        "count, in beats - so it",
        "scales with tempo. One",
        "beat by default: time",
        "to find the key. 2 or 4",
        "while a piece is new,",
        "1/4 when the rhythm is",
        "the point. Later than",
        "that still releases the",
        "scroll, but scores a",
        "miss.",
        "",
        "Guide pads lights the",
        "pad you need next. Off",
        "by default so you read",
        "rather than follow. It",
        "does nothing in the",
        "guessing modes.",
        "",
        "Any octave accepts the",
        "right note in the wrong",
        "register.",
        "",
        "Exercises live in the",
        "exercises folder. Add a",
        "JSON file and list it",
        "in index.json."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
